==Gameplay==
*The gameplay is quite simple. Just tap the unit on the bottom of the screen and it will send out that unit to face the enemy units. Also, tap the bottom right button to fire the cannon and tap the bottom left button to increase your worker level.

==Plot==
The plot begins the same as in the [[Ganso!! Nyanko Daisensou|original version]], but is extended with several additional chapters and modes, starting with two additional [[Empire of Cats]] Chapters.

==Characters==
===Cats===
*This game contains most of the Cat Units that are listed in the [[Cat Release Order]] and [[Cat Units]] pages.
*The first cats not from the original version are the earlier [[:Category:Special Cats|Special Cats]], such as the purchasable units and [[Valkyrie Cat (Special Cat)|Valkyrie Cat]].
*There are many cats exclusive to this version.

===Enemies===
*All enemies can be viewed in the [[Enemy Release Order]] and [[Enemy Dictionary]] pages.
*The first enemies not from the original version are [[Ms. Sign]], [[Dark Emperor Nyandam]] and [[Teacher Bun Bun]].
*There are many enemies exclusive to this version.

==Chapters and Stages==
The same as The Battle Cats in most parts, it has:
*[[Empire of Cats]]
*[[Into the Future]]
*[[Cats of the Cosmos]]
*[[The Aku Realms]]
*[[Stories of Legend]]
*[[Uncanny Legends]]
*[[Zero Legends]]
*[[Catclaw Dojo]]
*[[Special Events|Event Stages]]
*[[Collaboration Events|Collaboration Events]]
*[[Higher Score|Challenge Mode]]

==Ports==
The game has received multiple ports to other devices, including:
*3DS: [[The Battle Cats POP!|Tobidasu! Nyanko Daisensou]] (とびだす！にゃんこ大戦争, "Jump Out! Nyanko Great War") released in May 2015.
*PC: [[Minna de Nyanko Daisensou]] (みんなでにゃんこ大戦争, "Nyanko Great War with Everyone"), released in August 2017 but discontinued as of January 2019.
*Switch: [[The Battle Cats Unite!|Futari De! Nyanko Daisensou]] (ふたりで！にゃんこ大戦争, "Together! Nyanko Great War"), released in December 2018.

